<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-23">23 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth Blackwell becomes the first woman to earn a US medical degree</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Admitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> Medical College in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> almost as a joke, Blackwell graduated top of her class. She went on to found hospitals and a medical college for women.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charleston-south-carolina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charleston-south-carolina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-13">13 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nicholas Kelly leads a revolt at the Charleston workhouse</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An enslaved man named Nicholas Kelly led an insurrection in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charleston-south-carolina">Charleston, South Carolina</a>, wounding several guards with improvised weapons and freeing 37 enslaved people. Most were quickly captured, and Kelly and two others were tried and hanged.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charleston-south-carolina">Charleston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-orleans.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-15">15 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The steamboat Louisiana blows up as she leaves a New Orleans dock</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">All the boilers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> steamboat exploded about five minutes after she pulled away from the dock at Gravier Street, and she sank ten minutes later. At least 150 and possibly 200 people died, some of them on the steamer Storm alongside.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/surrender-at-vilagos" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/surrender-at-vilagos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/surrender-at-vilagos">Surrender at Világos</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Surrender at Világos took place on 13 August 1849, when the Hungarian army under Artúr Görgei laid down its arms to the Russian forces that had intervened on the Austrian side.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-revolution-of-1848" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungarian-revolution-of-1848.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-revolution-of-1848">Hungarian Revolution of 1848</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hungarian Revolution of 1848 was an uprising seeking Hungarian autonomy and then independence from Habsburg rule, part of the wider revolutions of 1848 in Europe.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-carreras" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-carreras.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-carreras">Battle of Las Carreras</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Las Carreras was fought in April 1849 near Baní in the Dominican Republic, where Dominican forces under Pedro Santana defeated the invading Haitian army of President Faustin Soulouque.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rebellion-losses-bill" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rebellion-losses-bill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rebellion-losses-bill">Rebellion Losses Bill</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rebellion Losses Bill was a law passed by the Province of Canada in 1849 to compensate residents of Canada East whose property had been damaged during the rebellions of 1837–1838.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/annexation-of-the-punjab">Annexation of the Punjab</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The annexation of the Punjab was the incorporation of the Sikh Empire's territory into British India by the East India Company in 1849.</p></div></li></ol></section>
